.TH CURLDBG 1 "May 2026" "curldbg" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
curldbg \- tiny HTTP/HTTPS request debugger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B curldbg
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIurl\fR
.P
.B curldbg
--compare [\fIoptions\fR] \fIurl\fR
.P
.B curldbg
--compare-urls [\fIoptions\fR] \fIurl-a\fR \fIurl-b\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B curldbg
performs a single HTTP/HTTPS request (GET/POST/PUT), reports timing metrics,
and prints a short preview of the response body. It can also compare IPv4 vs
IPv6 or compare two URLs side-by-side.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-L
Follow redirects.
.TP
.B \-4
Force IPv4.
.TP
.B \-6
Force IPv6.
.TP
.B \-X, \-\-request \fIGET|POST|PUT\fR
Choose HTTP method.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-data \fIbody\fR
Send request body (defaults method to POST if \-X is not set).
.TP
.B \-T, \-\-upload-file \fIfile\fR
Upload file as the PUT request body (single request mode only).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-fail
Exit non-zero on HTTP status >= 400.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-silent
Suppress normal output.
.TP
.B \-S, \-\-show-error
Show errors when used with \-s.
.TP
.B \-k, \-\-insecure
Skip TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-user \fIuser:pass\fR
Use HTTP Basic auth.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-header \fIheader\fR
Add a request header (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIfile\fR
Write response body to file (single request mode only).
.TP
.B \-O, \-\-remote-name
Write response body using the URL filename (single request mode only).
.TP
.B \-\-connect-timeout \fIms\fR
Timeout per connect attempt in milliseconds.
.TP
.B \-\-read-timeout \fIms\fR
Timeout for read/write operations in milliseconds.
.TP
.B \-\-max-redirs \fIn\fR
Maximum redirects when \-L is enabled.
.TP
.B \-\-compare
Compare IPv4 vs IPv6 for a single URL.
.TP
.B \-\-compare-urls
Compare two URLs side-by-side.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and author.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B curldbg \-L https://example.com
Follow redirects and print timing.
.TP
.B curldbg \-u user:pass \-H "Accept: application/json" https://example.com
Use Basic auth and custom header.
.TP
.B curldbg \-T ./file.bin https://example.com/upload
Upload a file using PUT.
.TP
.B curldbg \-\-compare https://example.com
Compare IPv4 vs IPv6 for one URL.
.SH AUTHOR
Pau Santana.
